---
import SiteLayout from "@layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Work – Good job."
  description="Design and development work by John Basham."
  home={false}
>
  <div class="archive-page">
    <article
      class="hentry page post-395 status-publish type-page"
      id="post-395"
      itemscope
      itemtype="https://schema.org/BlogPosting"
      role="article"
    >
      <header class="article-header">
        <h1 class="page-title" itemprop="headline">
          Work
        </h1>
      </header>
      <section class="entry-content" itemprop="articleBody">
        <h2 class="wp-block-heading">Case Studies</h2>
        <div
          class="alignwide is-stacked-on-mobile wp-block-media-text"
          style="grid-template-columns: 31% auto"
        >
          <figure class="wp-block-media-text__media">
            <img
              alt=""
              class="size-full wp-image-176"
              decoding="async"
              fetchpriority="high"
              height="633"
              sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px"
              src="/uploads/2018/11/case-study-emma-power-1024x633.jpg"
              srcset="
                      /uploads/2018/11/case-study-emma-power-1024x633.jpg 1024w,
                      /uploads/2018/11/case-study-emma-power-300x185.jpg   300w,
                      /uploads/2018/11/case-study-emma-power-768x475.jpg   768w,
                      /uploads/2018/11/case-study-emma-power.jpg          1650w
                    "
              width="1024"
            />
          </figure>
          <div class="wp-block-media-text__content">
            <h2 class="wp-block-heading">
              <a href="/emma-power/">Emma Power</a>
            </h2>
            <p>
              As a teacher, writer and speaker Emma had a simple request for her
              website – “simple and easy to navigate”.
            </p>
            <p class="has-text-align-right">
              <a href="/emma-power/">read more</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          class="alignwide is-stacked-on-mobile wp-block-media-text"
          style="grid-template-columns: 31% auto"
        >
          <figure class="wp-block-media-text__media">
            <img
              alt=""
              class="size-full wp-image-57"
              decoding="async"
              height="633"
              sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px"
              src="/uploads/2019/05/case-study-sunny-copy-cmps-1024x633.jpg"
              srcset="
                      /uploads/2019/05/case-study-sunny-copy-cmps-1024x633.jpg 1024w,
                      /uploads/2019/05/case-study-sunny-copy-cmps-300x185.jpg   300w,
                      /uploads/2019/05/case-study-sunny-copy-cmps-768x475.jpg   768w,
                      /uploads/2019/05/case-study-sunny-copy-cmps.jpg          1650w
                    "
              width="1024"
            />
          </figure>
          <div class="wp-block-media-text__content">
            <h2 class="wp-block-heading">
              <a href="/sunny-copy/">Sunny Copy</a>
            </h2>
            <p>
              Copywriting is all in the words. That’s why when you visit
              sunnycopy.com you won’t find anything fancy, just a beautiful and
              clean website. And beautiful words.
            </p>
            <p class="has-text-align-right">
              <a href="/sunny-copy/">read more</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          class="alignwide is-stacked-on-mobile wp-block-media-text"
          style="grid-template-columns: 31% auto"
        >
          <figure class="wp-block-media-text__media">
            <img
              alt="Screenshot of the homepage"
              class="size-full wp-image-174"
              decoding="async"
              height="633"
              sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px"
              src="/uploads/2018/12/case-study-jenna-meade-1650-1024x633.jpg"
              srcset="
                      /uploads/2018/12/case-study-jenna-meade-1650-1024x633.jpg 1024w,
                      /uploads/2018/12/case-study-jenna-meade-1650-300x185.jpg   300w,
                      /uploads/2018/12/case-study-jenna-meade-1650-768x475.jpg   768w,
                      /uploads/2018/12/case-study-jenna-meade-1650.jpg          1650w
                    "
              width="1024"
            />
          </figure>
          <div class="wp-block-media-text__content">
            <h2 class="wp-block-heading">
              <a href="/jenna-meade/">Jenna Meade</a>
            </h2>
            <p>
              Jenna is an Australian wellness travel journalist that needed a
              home for her writing. We designed and built her website to radiate
              her personality and make reading her words an absolute pleasure.
            </p>
            <p class="has-text-align-right">
              <a href="/jenna-meade/">read more</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          class="alignwide is-stacked-on-mobile wp-block-media-text"
          style="grid-template-columns: 31% auto"
        >
          <figure class="wp-block-media-text__media">
            <img
              alt=""
              class="size-full wp-image-314"
              decoding="async"
              height="319"
              loading="lazy"
              sizes="(max-width: 474px) 100vw, 474px"
              src="/uploads/2019/06/logo-thumbnail.jpg"
              srcset="
                      /uploads/2019/06/logo-thumbnail.jpg         474w,
                      /uploads/2019/06/logo-thumbnail-300x202.jpg 300w
                    "
              width="474"
            />
          </figure>
          <div class="wp-block-media-text__content">
            <h2 class="wp-block-heading">
              <a href="/soul-charters/">Soul Charters</a>
            </h2>
            <p>
              The duo behind Soul Charters are big dreamers. Capturing their
              dreams and encapsulating them into a website was a challenge worth
              waking up for.
            </p>
            <p class="has-text-align-right">
              <a href="/soul-charters/">read more</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          aria-hidden="true"
          class="wp-block-spacer"
          style="height: 100px"
        ></div>
        <h2 class="wp-block-heading">Branding</h2>
      </section>
      <section class="branding" itemprop="articleBody">
        <figure>
          <img
            height="197"
            src="/uploads/2021/10/logo-sunny_desktop_x2.png"
            width="330"
            alt=""
          />
        </figure>

        <figure>
          <img
            height="197"
            src="/uploads/2021/10/logo-retrea_desktop_x2.jpg"
            width="330"
            alt=""
          />
        </figure>

        <figure>
          <img
            height="197"
            src="/uploads/2021/10/logo-soulfuel_desktop_x2.png"
            width="330"
            alt=""
          />
        </figure>

        <figure>
          <img
            height="197"
            src="/uploads/2021/10/logo-vifplastics_desktop_x2.png"
            width="330"
            alt=""
          />
        </figure>

        <figure>
          <img
            height="197"
            src="/uploads/2021/10/logo-radical_desktop_x2.png"
            width="330"
            alt=""
          />
        </figure>

        <figure>
          <img
            height="197"
            src="/uploads/2021/10/logo-autotelic_desktop_x2.png"
            width="330"
            alt=""
          />
        </figure>

        <figure>
          <img
            height="197"
            src="/uploads/2021/10/logo-concreteworkshop_desktop_x2.png"
            width="330"
            alt=""
          />
        </figure>

        <figure>
          <img
            height="197"
            src="/uploads/2021/10/logo-billy_desktop_x2.png"
            width="330"
            alt=""
          />
        </figure>

        <figure>
          <img
            height="197"
            src="/uploads/2021/10/logo-acceleron_desktop_x2.png"
            width="330"
            alt=""
          />
        </figure>
        <img />
      </section>
      <section class="entry-content" itemprop="articleBody">
        <h2 class="wp-block-heading" style="margin-bottom:50px;">
          Brand Motion
        </h2>
        <div
          class="alignwide is-stacked-on-mobile wp-block-media-text"
          style="grid-template-columns: 31% auto"
        >
          <figure class="wp-block-media-text__media">
            <div class="featured-video">
              <video autoplay loop muted>
                <source
                  src="/uploads/2019/06/motion-promotion.mp4"
                  type="video/mp4"
                />
                <p>Sorry, your browser doesn't support embedded videos.</p>
              </video>
            </div>
          </figure>
          <div class="wp-block-media-text__content">
            <p>
              Give me 5 seconds – and I’ll bring your brand to life. Motion is
              powerful, often overlooked, and adds new depth of emotion to you
              and your brand.
            </p>
            <p>
              Most animated logos are made using preset motion templates that
              reveal the logo in a fancy way. While the effects can be
              impressive, they are ultimately generic and don’t add to your
              brand’s story. 
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          class="alignwide is-stacked-on-mobile wp-block-media-text"
          style="grid-template-columns: 31% auto"
        >
          <figure class="wp-block-media-text__media">
            <figure class="wp-block-video">
              <video
                autoplay
                loop
                muted
                poster="/uploads/2019/03/logo-heart.png"
                src="/uploads/2019/06/Comp-1_1.mp4"
              ></video>
            </figure>
          </figure>
          <div class="wp-block-media-text__content">
            <blockquote class="is-layout-flow is-style-default wp-block-quote wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
              <p>
                Animation provides a universal language to imbue emotion,
                augment feeling, and explain hard concepts.
              </p>
              <cite>Ryan McLeod</cite>
            </blockquote>
            <p>
              That’s where I step in. I add a layer of contextual and memorable
              motion that connects to your brand and its ethos. While your
              existing flat logo makes a first impression, your animated logo
              works one step harder to unveil clues and context about your
              offering.
            </p>
            <p>
              It’s storytelling that’s obvious, felt, and nearly invisible all
              at once. The finishing flowing touch to your narrative.
            </p>

            <hr style="margin:50px;opacity: .1; border: 0; height: 1px; background-color: #111;" />
            <b>Where to use...</b>
            <p>
              <strong>Social Media</strong> – Feeds are a perfect medium to
              stand out. Animation is far more memorable leaving a lasting
              impression.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Email Signature</strong> – There’s no more memorable way
              to sign off your email than with an animated logo. It shows you’ve
              cared enough to think about the small details.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Promotional Video</strong> – Spliced into the beginning or
              end, it adds another level of customised professionalism to your
              video content.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Website</strong> – Can easily be integrated into your
              website with great effect.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
